From: Bellatrix Project <bellatrix@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth prefs: use our own icon, not Trident's

Upstream ships Trident's icon as Prefs/Bluetooth.info and says so:

    # Placeholder icon (reuses the Trident prefs icon) so the program is
    # clickable in the Prefs drawer; a dedicated Bluetooth icon is a follow-up.

Trident is Poseidon's USB preferences, so on a machine that has both, two
unrelated programs sit in the Prefs drawer wearing the same face.

This is the icon that was drawn for BTScan in aros-bluzing -- the same
project whose stack upstream imported as rom/bluetooth/stack, licensed
LICENSE.aros-bluzing. Upstream took the banner (prefs/bluzinglogo) and left
the icon behind; this puts it back.

A 64x64 RGBA PNG icon with an icOn chunk typing it WBTOOL, rather than a
classic planar .info -- which is what BTScan.info always was, and it
rendered in Wanderer on this hardware.
---
diff --git a/rom/bluetooth/prefs/Bluetooth.info b/rom/bluetooth/prefs/Bluetooth.info
index e4d99378e643f40d19cfcfd0ff9321e949916427..bbb53f2dddcf3c84474273bbc775893540e71faa 100644
GIT binary patch
